{
  "title": "AssetFactoryContext",
  "description": "What a factory is told about the one resource it is building. There is deliberately no network, cache store or cache policy here. A factory receives source data that has already been acquired and decoded, and its only outward reach is dependencies - which acquires other ASSETS, never raw bytes. Where those bytes came from, and whether they were served from a cache, is not a factory's decision to make or to observe.",
